Package: infinite-streaming-boa
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Jonathan Oliver <jonathaneoliver@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Depends: iproute2, nftables, iw, hostapd, rfkill, iperf3
Recommends: avahi-daemon
Suggests: tcpdump
Homepage: https://github.com/jonathaneoliver/infinite-streaming-boa
Description: per-device network link conditioner for a transparent bridge
 boa sits between an existing router and the devices under test as a
 transparent layer-2 bridge, and conditions each device's traffic
 independently -- rate, latency, jitter and loss, per direction -- from a
 web interface. It also drives the Wi-Fi link itself through hostapd: drop,
 deadzone, steer and gather a client between radios.
 .
 This package installs the daemon and its service. It does not build the
 bridge or write hostapd configurations: the service is enabled on install
 but started only once the bridge named in /etc/default/infinite-streaming-boa
 exists.
